the following are the best practices for documenting tax services:
Documenting the client's sophistication regarding the tax and accounting matters;
Documenting the recommendations and alternatives, if applicable;
Documenting a disclaimer that the CPA is not responsible for updates to the advice if guidance or law changes;
Documenting the responsibility for implementation rests with the client, and not the CPA; and
Documenting the tax advice for federal and other tax advice, including state, local, international, and nontax matters.
